RISC3D test kit 34 (prototype, 15 November 2026)
================================================

ROL chose how RISC3D gets a newer Mesa: Debian's own, from
trixie-backports, pinned so that only Mesa follows backports. Note
that backports now has Mesa 26.1.6 (not the 25.2 named before), and
that is what kit 33's newmesa script fetched this morning too.

riscos-risc3d 0.19-1 carries the two apt files that do this, and
rol-3d 0.19 logs which Mesa it found, using its old V3D workaround only
below Mesa 25.2.

Steps (RiSH's Root shell)
-----
 1. Unzip RISC3DTest into HardDisc4, replacing kit 33.
 2. Install, then upgrade Mesa:
      apt-get install /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/riscos-risc3d_0.19-1_arm64.deb
      apt-get update
      apt-get full-upgrade
    (or Configure > Updates, Check then Install, instead of the last two)
 3. Remove kit 33's test copy:
      rm -rf /opt/riscos/gl-test
 4. Verify:
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/verify /riscos/3d/recorded/ctx-477.r3d
 5. Play TORCS.

